{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     training/path — the shape of the curriculum, as four stages.
     Ported from NS-Design-System/templates/training-index.html §02.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ DUMMY CONTENT, and deliberately allowed to be. This is a MARKETING
     band, not the curriculum: four stages is an editorial claim about how the
     material is organised, the same kind of copy every partial in
     partials/home/ carries. The CURRICULUM itself — modules and lessons — is
     Ghost content and is never written into a template. That is the line, and
     training/modules.hbs is the other side of it.

     When stages become real they become tags with backing posts, exactly like
     modules, and this turns into a {{#get}}.

     THE READER IS CHOOSING WHERE TO ENTER, which is why every stop is a link.
     <ol>, not a row of divs: the order is the meaning.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <header class="ns-band__head">
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "The shape of it"}}</span>
            <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Four stages, each ending where the next begins"}}</h2>
            <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "You are choosing where to enter, not committing to the whole journey — every stage stands on its own."}}</p>
        </header>

        <ol class="ns-path">
            <li class="ns-path__stop">
                <span class="ns-path__node">01</span>
                <a class="ns-path__card" href="#modules">
                    <span class="ns-tthumb ns-tthumb--glyph">{{> "icons/books"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__title">{{t "Foundations"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__text">{{t "Objects, fields, relationships and the data model everything else sits on."}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li class="ns-path__stop">
                <span class="ns-path__node">02</span>
                <a class="ns-path__card" href="#modules">
                    <span class="ns-tthumb ns-tthumb--glyph">{{> "icons/lock-simple"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__title">{{t "Security and sharing"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__text">{{t "Who sees what, why, and what happens when a record is reparented."}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li class="ns-path__stop">
                <span class="ns-path__node">03</span>
                <a class="ns-path__card" href="#modules">
                    <span class="ns-tthumb ns-tthumb--glyph">{{> "icons/strategy"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__title">{{t "Automation"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__text">{{t "Declarative first: records, screens, schedules, and the limits of each."}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__meta"><span>{{t "Free"}}</span></span>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li class="ns-path__stop">
                <span class="ns-path__node">04</span>
                <a class="ns-path__card" href="#modules">
                    <span class="ns-tthumb ns-tthumb--glyph">{{> "icons/code"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__title">{{t "Development"}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__text">{{t "Governor limits as a budget, bulkification as a habit, tests as proof."}}</span>
                    <span class="ns-path__meta"><span>{{t "Mixed"}}</span></span>
                </a>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>
